		sections={
			{id=7348,title="Ji-Kun's Flock",body="Ji-Kun's young are located throughout the roost and progress through different stages of life. After a period of incubation Young Eggs of Ji-Kun will hatch into Hatchlings. When fed by Ji-Kun, the Hatchlings then mature into Fledglings. Both Fledgling Eggs and Mature Eggs will hatch into Juveniles."},
			{id=7349,title="Young Egg of Ji-Kun",body="Eggs in the lower nests located around Ji-Kun's roost will periodically hatch. Once the egg hatches, a Hatchling will emerge."},
			{id=7350,title="Hatchlings",body="Hatchlings will call for Ji-Kun to feed them shortly after spawning. If a Hatchling senses food nearby, it will attempt to feed. If a Hatchling successfully feeds, it will mature into a Fledgling."},
			{id=7783,title="Cheep",body="The Hatchling yells with all their might at their current target, inflicting $139296s1 Physical damage."},
			{id=7351,title="Fledglings",body="Fledglings attack random players and can spawn incubated eggs."},
			{id=7352,title="Lay Egg",body="Fledglings will lay eggs that are already incubated. When these eggs hatch they spawn a Juvenile."},
			{id=7353,title="Cheep",body="The Fledgling yells with all their might at a random target, inflicting $140570s1 Physical damage."},
			{id=7606,title="Mature Egg of Ji-Kun",body="Mature Eggs of Ji-Kun take longer to incubate and spawn a Juvenile when the incubation process is complete."},
			{id=7607,title="Juvenile",body="Juveniles quickly take to the air and fly over the main platform of Ji-Kun. Juveniles periodically cast Cheep at a random target for as long as they're alive."},
			{id=7608,title="Cheep",body="The Juvenile screams with all their might, inflicting $140129s1 Physical damage to the victim."},
			{id=7827,title="Nest Guardians",body="On Heroic difficulty, some of Ji-Kun's nest are defended by Nest Guardians, which will attack any players attempting to disturb their nest.",difficultyIDs={5,6}},
			{id=7828,title="Talon Strike",body="The Nest Guardian strikes with both its talons, inflicting Physical damage to all enemies in a 180 degree arc.",difficultyIDs={5,6}},
			{id=7840,title="Screech",body="If not actively engaged in melee combat Nest Guardians will Screech, inflicting $140640s1 Physical damage and interrupting the current spellcast of all players. Mana-using players will have their casting speed reduced by $134372s1% until they successfully cast their next spell.",difficultyIDs={5,6}},
			{id=7856,title="Infected Talons",body="Whenever Ji-Kun successfully strikes a player with a melee ability the victim suffers $140092s1 Nature damage every $140092t seconds for $140092d. This effect stacks."},
			{id=7354,title="Feed Young",body="Ji-Kun spits up globs of food for her young. If a Hatchling has called out for food, Ji-Kun will aim this ability in their direction; otherwise the food will land at random locations around Ji-Kun's platform. When the food lands on the ground, it forms a Feed Pool.\n\nWhile a glob of food is traveling through the air, players with Flight can intercept it to prevent a Feed Pool from forming. Doing so afflicts the player with Slimed, but also grants Primal Nutriment."},
			{id=7355,title="Slimed",body="After intercepting Ji-Kun's food globules the player suffers $134256s1 Nature damage every $134256t seconds for $134256d. This effect increases the damage of the next Slimed by $138309s1% when it expires. The increased damage effect stacks."},
			{id=7834,title="Feed Pool",body="Feed Pools that form on the main platform will inflict $138319s1 Nature damage to all players within them each second. If a player stands in a Feed Pool for 3 seconds they will absorb the Feed Pool and become Slimed."},
			{id=7857,title="Primal Nutriment",body="Successfully catching one of Ji-Kun's food globules mid-air increases the player's damage by $140741s2% and healing by $140741s1% for $140741d. Primal Nutriment increases damage and healing by an additional 10% each time it is applied, up to a maximum of 200%."},
			{id=7364,title="Talon Rake",body="Ji-Kun uses her talons to pierce through the armor of her current target. Talon Rake inflicts $134366s2% weapon damage as Physical damage and increases the damage received by the victim from future Talon Rakes by $134366s1% for $134366d."},
			{id=7356,title="Quills",body="Ji-Kun sends her quills about the entire roost, inflicting $134381s1 Physical damage to all players every $134380t1 sec for $134380d."},
			{id=7370,title="Down Draft",body="Ji-Kun flaps her wings violently, pushing all enemies on her platform outward. Down Draft persists for $134370d."},
			{id=7357,title="Caw",body="Ji-Kun cries out at 1 random player, sending piercing sound waves at their location. When the waves reach their destination they inflict $134375s1 Physical damage to all targets within $134375A1 yards of the impact.",difficultyIDs={3,5}},
			{id=7358,title="Caw",body="Ji-Kun cries out at 3 random players, sending piercing sound waves at their locations. When the waves reach their destination they inflict $134375s1 Physical damage to all targets within $134375A1 yards of the impact.",difficultyIDs={4,6,7}},
			{id=7359,title="Daedalian Wings",body="When an egg or hatchling from the lower nests located around Ji-Kun's roost is slain it leaves behind a feather for players to loot. This feather grants the player Daedalian Wings. Daedalian Wings grants the player an extra action button that allows players to take flight for $133755d.\n\n$[!3,4 In Normal difficulty, feathers grant 4 charges of Daedalian Wings. Players can have up to 4 charges at any time.$]\n$[!5,6 In Heroic difficulty, feathers grant 3 charges of Daedalian Wings. Players can have up to 3 charges at any time.$]"},
			{id=7360,title="Flight",body="Players who have the Daedalian Wings buff can take flight for $133755d.\n$[!3,4,5,6 In the Normal and Heroic versions of the Ji-Kun encounter, using Flight consumes one charge of Daedalian Wings.$]"},
			{id=7835,title="Lesson of Icarus",body="After acquiring a feather, players must wait to acquire another.\n\n$[!3,4,5,6 In Normal and Heroic difficulties, players cannot gain further charges of Daedalian Wings for $140571d.$]\n$[!7 In Raid Finder difficulty, players can pick up (and only need) one Feather of Ji-Kun.$]"},
		},
	},
