			{itemID=112494,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112495,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112496,diffs={},faction=-1},
		},
		sections={
			{id=7939,title="Overview",body="Players battle the brewmaster Rook Stonetoe, the rogue He Softfoot, and the priest Sun Tenderheart, as the three Fallen Protectors assault the raid simultaneously.\n\nAt 66% and 33% health remaining, each Protector performs Desperate Measures, manifesting spirits of fallen allies to bring new and powerful attacks to bear against the raid until those spirits are defeated."},
			{id=10136,title="Damage Dealers",body="$bullet;Each Protector channels |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143497|h[Bond of the Golden Lotus]|h|r at 1% health remaining, and will recover unless all three are defeated at once.\n$bullet;Defeat the dark manifestations summoned by each Protector's Desperate Measures to end that phase.\n$bullet;During Rook's Desperate Measures, interrupt Embodied Gloom's |cFF2959D3|Hspell:144018|h[Corruption Shock]|h|r."},
			{id=10137,title="Healers",body="$bullet;Dispel Sun Tenderheart's |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143434|h[Shadow Word: Bane]|h|r quickly before it spreads.\n$bullet;During Sun Tenderheart's Desperate Measures, her |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143559|h[Dark Meditation]|h|r inflicts sustained damage to the entire raid."},
			{id=10138,title="Tanks",body="$bullet;If tanking Rook Stonetoe, position him carefully so that his |cFF2959D3|Hspell:144396|h[Vengeful Strikes]|h|r do not damage the raid.\n$bullet;If tanking He Softfoot, turn your back when he performs |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143301|h[Gouge]|h|r to avoid being incapacitated."},
			{id=8017,title="Bond of the Golden Lotus",body="Rook Stonetoe, He Softfoot, and Sun Tenderheart share a spiritual bond, linking their fates to each other. Upon reaching 1 health, each of them will begin to cast Bond of the Golden Lotus if any of the other Protectors are still in combat, restoring $143497s1% of maximum health upon completion.\n\nBringing all three Protectors to 1 health simultaneously will restore clarity to their clouded minds."},
			{id=7885,title="Rook Stonetoe"},
			{id=7956,title="Desperate Measures",body="Upon reaching 66% or 33% health remaining, Rook Stonetoe manifests evil forms of his closest friends, making Embodied Misery, Embodied Sorrow, and Embodied Gloom.\n\nOnce all three spirits are defeated, Rook Stonetoe resumes fighting players."},
			{id=8395,title="Embodied Misery"},
			{id=7958,title="Defiled Ground",body="Embodied Misery smashes the ground with fervor, inflicting $143961s1 Physical damage to her current target, knocking them back. This force burns into the ground, inflicting $144357s1 Shadow damage every second."},
			{id=8396,title="Embodied Sorrow"},
			{id=7959,title="Inferno Strike",body="Embodied Sorrow casts a massive Fire damage spell at a random target. Inferno Strike divides ${$143962m2*$143962m1} Fire damage among all targets within $143962A2 yards."},
			{id=8397,title="Embodied Gloom"},
			{id=7957,title="Corruption Shock",body="Embodied Gloom hurls a bolt of corrupted lightning at several locations, inflicting $144018s1 Nature damage to all enemies within $144018A1 yards."},
			{id=8330,title="Corruption Chain",body="On Heroic difficulty, Corruption Chain replaces Corruption Shock.\n\nEmbodied Gloom hurls a bolt of corrupted lightning at an enemy, inflicting $145631s1 Nature damage and chaining to enemies within 10 yards.",difficultyIDs={15,16}},
			{id=8331,title="Shared Torment",body="Embodied Misery, Sorrow, and Gloom share health.",difficultyIDs={16}},
			{id=8145,title="Vengeful Strikes",body="Rook Stonetoe enters an offensive stance, stunning his target and inflicting $144397s2 physical damage in a frontal cone twice per second for $144396D."},
			{id=7887,title="Corrupted Brew",body="Rook Stonetoe hurls a keg of Corrupted Brew at a distant target, inflicting $143023s1 Shadow damage to enemies within $143023A1 yards and slowing targets hit by $143023s2% for $143023d.$[!16\n\nIn Mythic difficulty, every two casts, Corrupted Brew's travel time is reduced by half a second. This effect resets when Rook Stonetoe begins his Desperate Measures.$]"},
			{id=7888,title="Clash",body="Rook Stonetoe clashes against an enemy, charging each other and meeting halfway. Rook Stonetoe then immediately begins to perform Corruption Kick.$[!14,15,17\n\nIn Non-Mythic Difficulty, Rook Stonetoe's Clash will not be cast during any Desperate Measures phase.$]"},
			{id=7886,title="Corruption Kick",body="Spins rapidly in a circle, rooting himself and inflicting $143009s1 Physical damage to targets within $143009A1 yards every second for $143007D. Additionally torments targets struck, inflicting $143010s1 Shadow damage every two seconds for $143010D."},
			{id=7889,title="He Softfoot"},
			{id=7940,title="Desperate Measures",body="Upon reaching 66% or 33% health remaining, He Softfoot manifests a twisted spirit of his brother, creating Embodied Anguish, which fixates upon the raid member who has the Mark of Anguish.\n\nOnce this spirit is defeated, He Softfoot resumes fighting players."},
			{id=7941,title="Mark of Anguish",body="Mark of Anguish periodically inflicts Shadow damage every second and roots the target. The Marked player gains the ability to transfer the Mark to another friendly player within $143842R yards.\n\nEmbodied Anguish's gaze moves to a random target upon killing his current target."},
			{id=7966,title="Shadow Weakness",body="When Embodied Anguish strikes targets, he applies Shadow Weakness, increasing damage taken by Mark of Anguish. Additionally, passing the Mark of Anguish applies one Shadow Weakness to all players. This effect stacks."},
			{id=8415,title="Debilitation",body="Possessing the Mark of Anguish debilitates targets, decreasing their armor by $147383s1% for $147383D."},
			{id=7901,title="Garrote",body="Traveling through the shadows, He Softfoot Garrotes targets, inflicting $143198s1 Physical damage every $143198T1 sec.\n\nThis effect is removed when He Softfoot begins his Desperate Measures."},
			{id=7902,title="Gouge",body="He Softfoot attempts to gouge the eyes of his target, incapacitating them for $143301D and fixating on a random target until Taunted. If the target is facing away, Gouge will instead knock them away a short distance."},
			{id=7892,title="Master Poisoner",body="He Softfoot is a Master Poisoner and occasionally coats his weapons with various types of poisons.$[!16\n\nIn Mythic Difficulty, Master Poisoner abilities also take effect when using Garrote or Fixate.$]$[!14,15,17\n\nIn Non-Mythic Difficulty, He Softfoot's Master Poisoner abilities will not be cast during any Desperate Measures phase.$]"},
			{id=7893,title="Noxious Poison",body="He Softfoot coats his weapon in a Noxious Poison, causing successful melee attacks to create pools of poison on the ground, inflicting $144367s1 Nature damage every second. These pools may be jumped over.\n\nThis effect is removed when He Softfoot begins his Desperate Measures."},
			{id=7894,title="Instant Poison",body="He Softfoot coats his weapon in an Instant Poison, causing successful melee attacks to inflict $143224s1 additional Nature damage."},
			{id=7904,title="Sun Tenderheart"},
			{id=7942,title="Desperate Measures",body="Upon reaching 66% or 33% health remaining, Sun Tenderheart manifests an evil form of her protectors, making Embodied Despair and Embodied Desperation.\n\nOnce both spirits are defeated, Sun Tenderheart resumes fighting players."},
			{id=7954,title="Dark Meditation",body="Sun Tenderheart enters a Dark Meditation, inflicting Shadow damage to all enemies every half second. Players take $143564s1% less damage from Dark Meditation when inside her Meditative Field."},
			{id=7943,title="Manifest Emotions",body="Embodied Despair and Embodied Desperation focus their negative emotions, creating Sha manifestations which attack players. Any damage taken by these manifested emotions will also be suffered by the creature that spawned them."},
			{id=7944,title="Meditation Spike",body="Sun Tenderheart periodically fires a bolt of dark energy that inflicts $143602s1 Shadow damage upon impact to enemies within $143602A1 yards."},
			{id=7905,title="Sha Sear",body="Causes an explosion of Shadow magic around the target, inflicting increasing Shadow damage every second to all enemies within $143424A2 yards around the target."},
			{id=7906,title="Shadow Word: Bane",body="Expels a word of misery upon multiple targets, inflicting $143434s2 Shadow damage every $143434T2 sec for $143434d. Each time this effect deals damage, it will jump to an additional target, up to a total of $143434s1 times."},
			{id=7907,title="Calamity",body="Calls forth a great Calamity, striking all players for $143493s1% of their maximum health as Shadow damage. This also removes Shadow Word: Bane from all targets.$[!16\n\nIn Mythic difficulty, Calamity increases in magnitude by an additional $143493s2% of maximum health each addtional time it is cast. This effect resets when Sun Tenderheart begins her Desperate Measures.$]$[!14,15,17\n\nIn Non-Mythic Difficulty, Sun Tenderheart's Calamity will not be cast during any Desperate Measures phase.$]"},
		},
	},
	[850]={
		encounterID=850,
		instanceID=369,
		order=8,
		name="General Nazgrim",
		lore="Once a grunt in service of the former warchief, Thrall, General Nazgrim rose quickly through the ranks after overwhelming victories in Grizzly Hills and the sunken city of Vashj'ir. Fiercely loyal to the Horde and bound by a rigorous code of honor and duty, Nazgrim will hold the line for his warchief until his dying breath.",
		dungeonEncounterID=1603,
		uiMapID=562,
		pin={x=0.6526,y=0.7355},
		difficultyIDs={14,15,16,17,241},
		npcIDs={60149,61682,66656,66961},
		displayIDs={48995},
		loot={
			{itemID=99720,diffs={16},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99721,diffs={16},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99722,diffs={16},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99667,diffs={17},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99680,diffs={17},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99745,diffs={14},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99681,diffs={17},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99746,diffs={14},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99682,diffs={15},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99747,diffs={14},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99687,diffs={15},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99692,diffs={15},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112778,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112779,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112780,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112781,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112782,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112783,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112785,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112787,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112788,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112789,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112790,diffs={},faction=-1},
		},
		sections={
			{id=10213,title="Overview",body="General Nazgrim is a powerful warrior who builds Rage by damaging players with various abilities, and periodically spends that Rage to unleash powerful attacks. Throughout the encounter, mixed groups of three Kor'kron troops at a time stream in to assist their General."},
			{id=10214,title="Damage Dealers",body="$bullet;Defeat Kor'kron Forces quickly so as not to get overwhelmed.\n$bullet;Interrupt Kor'kron Arcweavers' and Warshaman's spellcasts.\n$bullet;Quickly destroy Nazgrim's |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143536|h[Kor'kron Banner]|h|r and Warshaman's Healing Tide Totem when they are placed.\n$bullet;Directly attacking Nazgrim when he is in |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143593|h[Defensive Stance]|h|r will cause him to generate Rage rapidly."},
			{id=10215,title="Healers",body="$bullet;If General Nazgrim has between 75 and 99 Rage when Cooling Off ends, his |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143503|h[War Song]|h|r will deal heavy damage to the entire raid.\n$bullet;Kor'kron Assassins fixate on a non-tank target and deal heavy damage to their prey."},
			{id=10216,title="Tanks",body="$bullet;Trade off tanking Nazgrim to allow |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143494|h[Sundering Blow]|h|r to fade, or Nazgrim will gain large amounts of Rage.\n$bullet;Keep Kor'kron Warshaman far away from Nazgrim, or they may heal him significantly."},
			{id=7908,title="Sundering Blow",body="A powerful strike inflicts $143494s1 Physical damage and sunders the target's armor, reducing armor by $143494s2% for $143494d. Generates $143494s3 Rage plus $143494s3 additional Rage per stack of Sundering Blow on the target."},
			{id=7919,title="Bonecracker",body="Fling a heavy mace at a player to crack their bones, reducing maximum health by $143638s1% and causing the player to bleed for $143638s2 Physical damage every $143638t2 sec for $143638d."},
			{id=7913,title="Execute",body="Executes a player for $143502s1 Physical damage. This attack pierces immunities and cannot be dodged, blocked, or parried.",difficultyIDs={16}},
			{id=7915,title="Stances",body="General Nazgrim will take on various stances during the battle."},
			{id=7916,title="Battle Stance",body="A balanced stance that generates $143589s1 Rage every $143589t1 sec."},
			{id=7917,title="Berserker Stance",body="A wild stance that increases damage dealt by $143594s1%, damage taken by $143594s2%, and Rage generated by $143594s3%."},
			{id=7918,title="Defensive Stance",body="A defensive stance that reduces damage taken by $143593s1% and grants $143597s1 Rage when struck. Rage gain cannot occur more than once every one second.\n\nAttacks by players affected by Sundering Blow do not cause Nazgrim to generate Rage."},
			{id=7909,title="Rage",body="Several of General Nazgrim's abilities require Rage to use. General Nazgrim will gain Rage from various abilities used during the battle.\n\nGeneral Nazgrim prefers to use the ability with the highest Rage cost."},
			{id=7910,title="Heroic Shockwave",body="Leaps at a player, inflicts $143716s1 Physical damage within $143716A1 yards of the impact location and causing three Aftershocks.\n\nCosts 30 Rage."},
			{id=7911,title="Aftershock",body="The ground cracks between General Nazgrim's impact location and the location a player target. After several seconds, the cracks will erupt, inflicting $143712s1 Fire damage to players within the Aftershock and granting General Nazgrim $143590s1 Rage for each player struck."},
			{id=7912,title="Kor'kron Banner",body="Places a banner that causes allies' attacks to generate $143590s1 Rage for General Nazgrim.\n\nCosts 50 Rage."},
			{id=7914,title="War Song",body="Unleash a hellish scream, inflicting $143503s1% of maximum health as Physical damage to all players.\n\nCosts 70 Rage."},
			{id=7938,title="Ravager",body="Throw a whirling blade that inflicts $143873s1 Physical damage to enemies within $143873A1 yards every $143874t1 sec, granting General Nazgrim $143877s1 Rage for each enemy struck.\n\nCosts 100 Rage."},
			{id=7937,title="Cooling Off",body="After using an ability that costs Rage, General Nazgrim must cool off for $143484d. During this time, General Nazgrim cannot use abilities that cost Rage."},
			{id=7920,title="Kor'kron Forces",body="General Nazgrim will call for the aid of his forces during the battle.\n\nAt 10% health, General Nazgrim will call in an additional wave of forces."},
			{id=7921,title="Orgrimmar Faithful",body="General Nazgrim begins the battle with a contingent of loyalist Orgrimmar grunts."},
			{id=7922,title="Kor'kron Ironblade",body="Kor'kron Ironblades wield a fierce two-handed blade."},
			{id=7926,title="Ironstorm",body="Whirl around in a storm of iron, inflicting $143421s1 Physical damage to players within $143421A1 yards every $143420t1 sec. for $143420d."},
			{id=7927,title="Last Stand",body="Increases maximum health by $143427s1%. Kor'kron Ironblades will use Last Stand when brought below 50% health."},
			{id=7923,title="Kor'kron Arcweaver",body="Kor'kron Arcweavers have mastered the arcane arts."},
			{id=7928,title="Arcane Shock",body="Shock a target, inflicting $143432s1 Arcane damage and increasing Arcane damage dealt by the caster by $143432s2% for $143432d. Stacks up to $143432u times."},
			{id=7929,title="Magistrike",body="Calls down a burst of Arcane energy, inflicting $143431s1 Arcane damage instantly and $143431s2 Arcane damage every $143431t2 sec. for $143431d to enemies within $143431A1 yards."},
			{id=7930,title="Unstable Blink",body="Teleport 1-2 times in a random direction."},
			{id=7924,title="Kor'kron Assassin",body="Kor'kron Assassins strike from the shadows at the enemy's weakest targets."},
			{id=7931,title="Stealth",body="Kor'kron Assassins begin the battle in stealth.  Slows movement speed by $118969s2%."},
			{id=7932,title="Backstab",body="Inflicts $143481s1 Physical damage to a player, but only if attacking from behind."},
			{id=7933,title="Assassin's Mark",body="Kor'kron Assassins will fixate on a non-tank target."},
			{id=7925,title="Kor'kron Warshaman",body="Kor'kron Warshaman specialize in aiding their allies."},
			{id=7934,title="Earth Shield",body="Protects the target with an earthen shield that heals the shielded target for $143479s1% of maximum health when damage is taken."},
			{id=7935,title="Empowered Chain Heal",body="Heals an ally for $143473s1% of their maximum health and jumps to a nearby ally, increasing healing by 50% per jump. Affects $143473x1 total targets."},
			{id=7936,title="Healing Tide Totem",body="Summons a totem that heals allies within $143478A1 yards for $143478s1% of their maximum health every $143477t1 sec."},
			{id=7946,title="Kor'kron Sniper",difficultyIDs={16}},
			{id=7947,title="Hunter's Mark",body="Kor'kron Snipers will fixate on a non-tank target."},
			{id=7948,title="Shoot",body="Shoots a player, inflicting $143884s1% weapon damage."},
			{id=7949,title="Multi-Shot",body="Fire a volley of arrows, inflicting $143887s1 Physical damage to enemies within a $143887A1-yard cone."},
		},
	},
	[851]={
		encounterID=851,
		instanceID=369,
		order=11,
		name="Thok the Bloodthirsty",
		lore="When the Isle of Giants was discovered off the coast of Pandaria, teeming with primal devilsaurs, Garrosh sent troops to capture some of the most fearsome specimens, hoping to subjugate them and use them as beasts of war. Countless orcish beastmasters have fallen to Thok's jaws as they struggle to tame him, yet the creature's thirst for blood remains unslaked.",
		dungeonEncounterID=1599,
		uiMapID=564,
		pin={x=0.513,y=0.8213},
		difficultyIDs={14,15,16,17,241},
		npcIDs={71529},
		displayIDs={49082,51144},
		loot={
			{itemID=99723,diffs={16},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99724,diffs={16},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99725,diffs={16},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99671,diffs={17},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99672,diffs={17},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99673,diffs={17},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99683,diffs={15},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99748,diffs={14},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99749,diffs={14},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99750,diffs={14},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99689,diffs={15},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99694,diffs={15},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112849,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112850,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112851,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112852,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112853,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112854,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112855,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112856,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112861,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112862,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112866,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=105357,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=105602,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=105604,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=105608,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=105609,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=105610,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=105611,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=216548,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=216554,diffs={},faction=-1},
		},
		sections={
			{id=10234,title="Overview",body="Thok alternates between two modes. When initially engaged, he performs Deafening Screech with increasing frequency, dealing heavy raidwide damage. When he detects a clump of seriously injured players, Thok enters a Blood Frenzy, during which he pursues random targets, instantly devouring any players that cross his path. During Blood Frenzy, he moves faster and faster; defeating a Kor'kron Jailer and freeing a prisoner for Thok to devour will empower him but end his Blood Frenzy."},
			{id=10235,title="Damage Dealers",body="$bullet;Avoid Thok's hungering jaws during his |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143442|h[Blood Frenzy]|h|r, or perish instantly.\n$bullet;Defeat the Kor'kron Jailer that emerges during Thok's |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143442|h[Blood Frenzy]|h|r.\n$bullet;If an ally is frozen by Thok's |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143800|h[Icy Blood]|h|r, destroy the ice block to free them."},
			{id=10236,title="Healers",body="$bullet;Time your spellcasts carefully to avoid being interrupted by Thok's |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143343|h[Deafening Screech]|h|r.\n$bullet;Avoid Thok's hungering jaws during his |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143442|h[Blood Frenzy]|h|r, or perish instantly.\n$bullet;Dispel |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143791|h[Corrosive Blood]|h|r from allies."},
			{id=10237,title="Tanks",body="$bullet;Take turns tanking Thok to allow the effects of his breath attacks to fade.\n$bullet;Orient Thok carefully to avoid hitting your allies with either his breath attacks or his |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143428|h[Tail Lash]|h|r.\n$bullet;Avoid Thok's hungering jaws during his |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143442|h[Blood Frenzy]|h|r, or perish instantly."},
			{id=7960,title="Stage 1: A Cry in the Darkness"},
			{id=7962,title="Fearsome Roar",body="Thok's bellowing roar inflicts $143426s1 Physical damage in a frontal cone. The roar incites terror in players' hearts, causing them to take $143766s1% more damage per stack."},
			{id=7963,title="Deafening Screech",body="Upon reaching full energy, Thok lets loose a shrill cry, inflicting $143343s1 Physical damage to all enemies and interrupting spellcasts. Every time Thok Screeches, the rate of his energy regeneration is increased."},
			{id=7964,title="Tail Lash",body="Thok's mighty tail whips about, striking all enemies behind the caster, inflicting $143428s1 Physical damage and stunning them for $143428d."},
			{id=7965,title="Shock Blast",body="Electricity arcs and snaps around Thok's shock collar, inflicting $143707s1 Nature damage to random enemies."},
			{id=7967,title="Bloodied",body="When players fall beneath 50% health, Thok the Bloodthirsty can smell their blood. If at least half the players in the raid are within 10 yards of one another while Bloodied, the scent of blood becomes overwhelming and Thok enters a Blood Frenzy.",difficultyIDs={14,15,16}},
			{id=7961,title="Stage 2: Frenzy for Blood!",body="The excessive scent of blood sends Thok into a frenzy for blood!\n\n$[!17 In Raid Finder difficulty, this occurs when Thok reaches 80%, 55%, and 30% health. $]"},
			{id=7981,title="Blood Frenzy",body="Thok roars in hunger, knocking away front enemies and going into a frenzy for blood. Any enemies who are caught within reach of Thok's terrible maw are devoured instantly. \n\nThok gradually gains speed during Blood Frenzy. He is also immune to taunt during Blood Frenzy."},
			{id=7980,title="Fixate",body="Thok becomes unable to be tanked, and will fixate on random distant players."},
			{id=7968,title="Kor'kron Jailer",body="Thok's mighty roar when he enters a Blood Frenzy attracts the attention of a nearby jailer. Upon defeating him, you may obtain a prison key that can unlock one of the nearby cells containing Garrosh's prisoners."},
			{id=8581,title="Breaking Loose!",difficultyIDs={16}},
			{id=8582,title="Starved Yeti"},
			{id=8583,title="Wrecking Ball",body="The Starved Yeti charges to random locations, inflicting $148143s1 Physical damage and knocking back all players in its path."},
			{id=8584,title="Captive Cave Bat"},
			{id=8585,title="Vampiric Frenzy",body="A random cave bat will enter a vampiric frenzy, inflicting $147978s1 Physical damage to all enemies. A portion of this damage is returned to the caster as health."},
			{id=7969,title="Prisoners of War",body="Garrosh has taken prisoners during his Pandaria campaign, and they remain trapped in cages alongside the beasts, hoping for freedom."},
			{id=8283,title="Akolik",body="Akolik and a band of his Skumblade have been taken captive by Garrosh. Upon being freed, he will invoke the holy order of Kros to subdue a nearby dinosaur.\n\nIt has... unpredictable results."},
			{id=7973,title="An Infusion of Acid",body="Once Akolik draws Thok's attention, the mighty dinosaur will devour him and absorb the acidic powers of the saurok. This will end Thok's Blood Frenzy."},
			{id=7977,title="Acid Breath",body="Thok's Fearsome Roar is replaced by Acid Breath. Acid Breath inflicts $143780s1 Nature damage in a frontal cone. The acid coats the armor of affected players, reducing its effectiveness by $143780s2% per stack."},
			{id=7976,title="Corrosive Blood",body="A corrosive poison seeps from every one of Thok's pores. This toxin hits random players, inflicting $143791s1 Nature damage initially, and then $143791s2 Nature damage every $143791t2 sec for $143791d."},
			{id=8284,title="Waterspeaker Gorai",body="Waterspeaker Gorai and some denizens of Inkgill Mere have been taken captive by Garrosh. When freed, Waterspeaker Gorai will command his units to aid you, and he will heal the wounds of random players."},
			{id=7974,title="An Infusion of Frost",body="Once Gorai draws Thok's attention, the mighty dinosaur will devour him and absorb the watery powers of the jinyu. This will end Thok's Blood Frenzy."},
			{id=7978,title="Freezing Breath",body="Thok's Fearsome Roar is replaced by Freezing Breath. Freezing Breath inflicts $143426s1 Frost damage in a frontal cone and coats players in frost. After 5 stacks, the target will be frozen in a tomb of ice."},
			{id=7979,title="Icy Blood",body="Thok's skin freezes and cracks, spurting plumes of ice from within. Icy Blood inflicts $143800s1 Frost damage to random enemies and coats enemies in ice for $143800d. This ice inflicts $143773s3 damage every $143773t3 seconds.  Upon reaching 5 stacks of the debuff, a player becomes frozen in a tomb of ice."},
			{id=8285,title="Warmaster Montak",body="Warmaster Montak and his firesworn have been taken captive by Garrosh. When freed, nearby units will have their weapons set ablaze, giving them a chance to cause additional Fire damage on successful attacks."},
			{id=7975,title="An Infusion of Flame",body="Once Montak draws Thok's attention, the mighty dinosaur will devour him and absorb the fiery powers of the yaungol. This will end Thok's Blood Frenzy."},
			{id=7982,title="Scorching Breath",body="Thok's Fearsome Roar is replaced by Scorching Breath. Scorching Breath inflicts $143426s1 Fire damage in a frontal cone. The flames sear enemy flesh, causing $143767s2 Fire damage every $143767t2 seconds."},
			{id=7983,title="Burning Blood",body="Thok's skin becomes coated in a sheen of incendiary oil, inflicting $143783s1 Fire damage to random enemies and leaving a puddle of flame beneath their feet."},
		},
	},
	[852]={
		encounterID=852,
		instanceID=369,
		order=1,
		name="Immerseus",
		lore="The ancient inhabitants of Pandaria recognized the vital importance of the lifegiving Pools of Power, building an underground system of aqueducts to safeguard the waters and nurture life in the Vale of Eternal Blossoms. The touch of corruption has animated and twisted these waters, and Immerseus stands as an unnatural embodiment of the Vale's sorrow.",
		dungeonEncounterID=1602,
		uiMapID=557,
		pin={x=0.4196,y=0.4526},
		difficultyIDs={14,15,16,17,241},
		npcIDs={71543},
		displayIDs={49056},
		loot={
			{itemID=112416,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112417,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112418,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112419,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112420,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112421,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112422,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112423,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112424,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=110761,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112425,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112426,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112427,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112428,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112429,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112445,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112447,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=110784,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112448,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=110785,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112382,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112383,diffs={},faction=-1},
		},
		sections={
			{id=8334,title="Overview",body="Immerseus begins with 100 Corruption, displayed as a visible power bar, and the objective of the encounter is to cleanse him by reducing his Corruption level to 0. Each time Immerseus is reduced to zero health, he Splits into a mix of dark Sha Puddles and watery Contaminated Puddles. Following each Split, Immerseus reforms with reduced health and Corruption depending on how successful the raid was in dealing with the two types of Puddles. \n\nThis cycle repeats until Immerseus's Corruption reaches 10 or lower, at which point he is cleansed."},
			{id=10132,title="Damage Dealers",body="$bullet;Rotate away from Immerseus's |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143413|h[Swirl]|h|r ability.\n$bullet;When Immerseus splits, destroy the dark Sha Puddles before they reach the center and merge into Immerseus."},
			{id=10133,title="Healers",body="$bullet;Rotate away from Immerseus's |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143413|h[Swirl]|h|r ability.\n$bullet;When Immerseus splits, heal Contaminated Puddles to purify them before they reach the center and merge with Immerseus.\n$bullet;When Sha or Contaminated Puddles reach the central pool, each one triggers |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143498|h[Erupting Sha]|h|r, damaging the entire raid."},
			{id=10134,title="Tanks",body="$bullet;Point Immerseus away from the raid, and take turns tanking to mitigate the effects of |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143436|h[Corrosive Blast]|h|r.\n$bullet;When Immerseus splits, destroy the dark Sha Puddles before they reach the center and merge into Immerseus."},
			{id=7984,title="Tears of the Vale",body="As a water elemental, Immerseus attacks players directly."},
			{id=7985,title="Sha Bolt",body="Immerseus fires a Sha Bolt at every enemy, inflicting $143295s1 Shadow damage to enemies within $143295A1 yards, and forming a Sha Pool at the targeted location. Sha Pools inflict $143297s1 Shadow damage every second."},
			{id=7987,title="Swirl",body="Immerseus causes torrents of Sha-corrupted water to burst from beneath the cracks in the ground. Players that come into contact with the tainted waters will suffer $143413s1 Shadow damage and be knocked away."},
			{id=7988,title="Corrosive Blast",body="Immerseus inflicts $143436s1 Shadow damage in a cone aimed at his primary target, increasing Shadow damage taken by $143436s2% for $143436d. Stacks."},
			{id=7991,title="Seeping Sha",body="Coming into contact with the Seeping Sha that surrounds Immerseus inflicts $143286s1 Shadow damage and knocks players back."},
			{id=7989,title="Swelling Corruption",body="Immerseus surges with power, gaining stacks of Swelling Corruption proportional to his current Corruption level. This power lashes out at players who strike Immerseus with single target abilities, coalescing into a Congealed Sha creature as well as inflicting Sha Corruption upon the attacker, which deals at least $143579s1 Shadow damage every $143579t1 sec for $143579d, increasing in damage rapidly with each additional stack.",difficultyIDs={16}},
			{id=7992,title="Split",body="Upon reaching zero health, Immerseus becomes unstable and bursts into a shower of Sha Puddles and Contaminated Puddles, which will attempt to reform in the pool at the center of the chamber. \n\nFor each Sha Puddle killed and each Contaminated Puddle healed to full, Immerseus's Corruption is reduced by one."},
			{id=7993,title="Sha Puddle",body="When destablized, Immerseus forms one Sha Puddle for every four units of Corruption he has. Destroying a Sha Puddle before it merges back into the central pool will remove one unit of Corruption."},
			{id=7994,title="Sha Residue",body="When a Sha Puddle is destroyed, it triggers Sha Residue, applying Sha Residue to enemies within $143459A1 yards and increasing damage dealt to other Sha Puddles by $143459s2%. This effect stacks."},
			{id=7995,title="Contaminated Puddle",body="When destablized, Immerseus forms one Contaminated Puddle for every four units of Corruption that have previously been removed. Healing a Contaminated Puddle to full health before it merges back into the central pool will cause it to become Purified, and remove one unit of Corruption upon reaching Immerseus."},
			{id=7996,title="Congealing",body="The speed of the Contaminated Puddle wanes as it increases in health."},
			{id=7997,title="Purified Residue",body="Upon reaching full health, a Contaminated Puddle releases Purified Residue, restoring $143524s1% mana to allies within $143524A1 yards and increasing healing done by $143524s2%. This effect stacks."},
			{id=7998,title="Erupting Sha",body="When any Puddle reaches Immerseus, it triggers an eruption, inflicting $143498s1 Shadow damage to all players for a Sha or Contaminated Puddle, or $145377s1 Frost damage for a Purified Puddle."},
			{id=7999,title="Sha Pool",body="The Sha Pool grows over time, inflicting at least $119941s1 Shadow damage over $119941t1 sec to enemies who touch it, stacking and increasing rapidly in damage proportional to the number of stacks. Touching the Sha Pool causes it to shrink, whereas it will expand whenever any Puddle reaches it.",difficultyIDs={16}},
			{id=8000,title="Seeping Sha",body="Coming into contact with the Seeping Sha that surrounds Immerseus inflicts $143286s1 Shadow damage and knocks players back.",difficultyIDs={14,15,17}},
		},
	},
	[853]={
		encounterID=853,
		instanceID=369,
		order=13,
		name="Paragons of the Klaxxi",
		lore="The nine surviving Klaxxi'va Paragons are ancient champions of the mantid who fought alongside the Wakener against the madness of Empress Shek'zeer. But the paragons, as do all mantid, hold a far deeper loyalty. When Garrosh unearthed the heart of Y'Shaarj, the paragons followed the whispers of their ancient master to the iron halls beneath Orgrimmar.",
		dungeonEncounterID=1593,
		uiMapID=566,
		pin={x=0.6834,y=0.353},
		difficultyIDs={14,15,16,17,241},
		npcIDs={71152,71153,71154,71155,71156,71157,71158,71160,71161},
		displayIDs={48674,48675,48676,48677,48678,48679,48680,48681,48682},
		loot={
			{itemID=104165,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99712,diffs={16},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99713,diffs={16},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99726,diffs={16},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99674,diffs={17},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99675,diffs={17},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99676,diffs={17},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99684,diffs={15},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99751,diffs={14},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99752,diffs={14},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99688,diffs={15},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99753,diffs={14},faction=-1},
			{itemID=99693,diffs={15},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112913,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112914,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112915,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112916,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112917,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112918,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112919,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112920,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112921,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112922,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112923,diffs={},faction=-1},
		},
		sections={
			{id=10250,title="Overview",body="Three Klaxxi Paragons join the fight at the beginning of the encounter, while the remaining six observe the action from perches above. Each time a Klaxxi Paragon is defeated, any other active Paragons heal to full and the next Klaxxi Paragon leaps down to join the fight. The encounter ends when all nine have been defeated."},
			{id=10251,title="Damage Dealers",body="$bullet;Defeat the Blood oozes summoned by Skeer's |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143280|h[Bloodletting]|h|r before they can reach their target.\n$bullet;After Hisek |cFF2959D3|Hspell:142948|h[Aims]|h|r, he |cFF2959D3|Hspell:142950|h[Fires]|h|r, dealing massive damage split among all players in a line with the target.\n$bullet;When Korven is active, break the shell created by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:142564|h[Encase in Amber]|h|r or the targeted Paragon will be healed.\n$bullet;Kaz'tik's Hungry Kunchongs instantly devour anyone who touches them, except when feeding on a |cFF2959D3|Hspell:142668|h[Mesmerized]|h|r player."},
			{id=10252,title="Healers",body="$bullet;Rik'kal's Amber Parasites fixate on different players and deal heavy damage via |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143362|h[Feed]|h|r.\n$bullet;After Hisek |cFF2959D3|Hspell:142948|h[Aims]|h|r, he |cFF2959D3|Hspell:142950|h[Fires]|h|r, dealing massive damage split among all players in a line with the target.\n$bullet;Kaz'tik's Hungry Kunchongs instantly devour anyone who touches them, except when feeding on a |cFF2959D3|Hspell:142668|h[Mesmerized]|h|r player."},
			{id=10253,title="Tanks",body="$bullet;Rik'kal's |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143339|h[Injection]|h|r fails if you have an active mitigation ability in effect, and only spawns Parasites if Rik'kal is still alive when |cFF2959D3|Hspell:143339|h[Injection]|h|r expires.\n$bullet;Skeer and Rik'kal must be tanked by separate players, as must Xaril and Kil'ruk, as each Paragon afflicts a vulnerability to the other's attacks.\n$bullet;When a Hungry Kunchong reaches full Energy it will |cFF2959D3|Hspell:142651|h[Molt]|h|r and mature into a large kunchong that must be tanked."},
			{id=8001,title="Paragons of the Klaxxi"},
			{id=8002,title="Paragon's Purpose",body="Whenever a Klaxxi Paragon is defeated, all other active Klaxxi Paragons heal to full and gain a $143482s1% damage bonus.",difficultyIDs={14,15,17}},
			{id=8576,title="Paragon's Purpose",body="Whenever a Klaxxi Paragon is defeated all other active Klaxxi Paragons heal to full. \nAll active Paragons gain a stacking $143482s1% damage bonus every 50 seconds.",difficultyIDs={16}},
			{id=8003,title="Ready to Fight",body="Klaxxi Paragons with this aura on them will be the next to join the fight. \n\nBefore the fight begins, three Klaxxi Paragons will have this aura. When the encounter begins all three of these Paragons join the encounter and one other Paragon will gain this aura to indicate that they will join the fight next.\n\nEverytime a new Klaxxi Paragon joins the fight, one of the inactive Klaxxi Paragons will gain this aura."},
			{id=8074,title="Power of the Paragons",body="After a Paragon has been defeated, one player may take the fallen Paragon's powers to use as their own. Only one player can take any one Paragon's power, and a player may only take a Paragon's power once during the encounter.\n\nEach Paragon's powers can only be acquired by particular class roles."},
			{id=8014,title="Skeer the Bloodseeker"},
			{id=8061,title="Hewn",body="The attacks of Skeer the Bloodseeker leave the victim more susceptible to the meddling of Rik'kal the Dissector's attacks. The victim suffers $143275s1% more damage per application from Rik'kal the Dissector."},
			{id=8062,title="Bloodletting",body="Skeer swings his weapon in a mighty arc, inflicting Physical damage to the target and causing blood creatures to spawn around the room.\n\nEach blood moves to a Paragon and will heal that Paragon based on the remaining health of the blood.\n\n$[!3 In 10 Player Normal Difficulty 2 bloods are summoned.$]$[!4 In 25 Player Normal Difficulty 3 bloods are summoned.$]$[!5 In 10 Player Heroic Difficulty 3 bloods are summoned.$]$[!6 In 25 Player Heroic Difficulty 4 bloods are summoned.$]$[!7 In Raid Finder Difficulty 1 blood is summoned.$]$[!14 In Flexible Difficulty 2-3 bloods are summoned.$]"},
			{id=8081,title="Bloodthirsty",body="Players of the damage dealer role can acquire this Paragon Power. When activated all attacks over the next $143319d have a chance to spawn blood orbs that persist for $143321d. If any player walks through a blood orb they will heal for $143322s1% of their maximum health."},
			{id=8015,title="Rik'kal the Dissector"},
			{id=8063,title="Genetic Alteration",body="Rik'kal's meddling with his victim's genetic makeup leaves them more susceptible to the attacks of Skeer the Bloodseeker. Victims suffer an additional $143279s1% damage from Skeer the Bloodseeker for each application of Genetic Alteration."},
			{id=8064,title="Injection",body="Rik'kal Injects his victim with a virus that inflicts $143339s1 Nature damage per second per application. When the virus expires, several Parasites will burst from the victim and attack players at random.\n\nInjection will not hit tanks that are actively trying to mitigate damage.",difficultyIDs={14,15,16}},
			{id=8065,title="Amber Parasite",body="Amber Parasites are Genetically Modified and fixate on a random player when they spawn. The Amber Parasite Feeds on the fixated target."},
			{id=8066,title="Genetic Modifications",body="Rik'kal's Bioengineering abilities have given these parasites the ability to fully regenerate every 10 seconds."},
			{id=8067,title="Feed",body="Amber Parasites inflict $143362s1 Physical damage each second."},
			{id=8068,title="Mutate: Amber Scorpion",body="Rik'kal tosses a vial at a random player, causing them to mutate into an Amber Scorpion. While transformed, the victim suffers $143337s4 Fire damage per second and only has access to the abilities of an Amber Scorpion.\n\nDamage inflicted as an Amber Scorpion is based on the player's Attack Power, Ranged Attack Power, or Spell Power, whichever is largest."},
			{id=8069,title="Claw",body="Amber Scorpions can lash out with one of their claws for 100% damage."},
			{id=8070,title="Swipe",body="The Amber Scorpion sweeps both of its claws in front of it, inflicting 150% damage to all targets in the area. Targets currently under the effects of Sting suffer double damage."},
			{id=8071,title="Sting",body="The Amber Scorpion Stings the target, causing it to suffer Nature damage every second."},
			{id=8472,title="Prey",body="Mutated Scorpions can instantly kill an Amber Parasite with this ability.\n\n$[!5,6 In Heroic Difficulties mutated victims must use this ability or perish from Faulty Mutation.$]"},
			{id=8473,title="Faulty Mutation",body="In Heroic Difficulties, mutated victims suffer a Faulty Mutation. If the victim fails to Prey on an Amber Parasite before the Faulty Mutation expires they will perish.",difficultyIDs={16}},
			{id=8082,title="Mad Scientist",body="Players of any role can acquire this Paragon Power. When activated the caster mutates into a giant amber scorpion. Damage inflicted by the scorpion is based on the highest available attack or spell power of the caster. While mutated the caster suffers $143373s5 Physical damage per second from the shock. The mutation lasts for $143373d."},
			{id=8016,title="Hisek the Swarmkeeper"},
			{id=8072,title="Multi-Shot",body="Hisek the Swarmkeeper fires a shot at several random players for Physical damage."},
			{id=8474,title="Rapid Fire",body="Hisek fires several volleys in rapid succession, with each successive volley moving slightly faster than the previous one. Players caught in the path of the volleys suffer $143240s1 Physical damage each second they are in the volley.",difficultyIDs={16}},
			{id=8073,title="Aim",body="Hisek the Swarmkeeper selects a player at random and stuns them for $142948d. If the target is too close they will be knocked back until they are 45 yards from Hisek.\n\nAfter Hisek is finished aiming at the target he will Fire a beam of $142950s2 Physical damage at all targets between him and the victim. Damage is shared between all targets equally and each target hit by the beam will create a field of Sonic Resonance at their location that inflicts $144094s1 Physical damage to all targets within $144094A1 yards of the victim."},
			{id=8083,title="Compound Eye",body="Players of the damage dealer role can acquire this Paragon Power. When activated, the player fires a shot at the target that inflicts greater Physical damage the further away the target is. Successfully hitting the target afflicts it with Marked for Death, increasing its damage taken by $143218s1% for $143218d."},
			{id=8013,title="Ka'roz the Locust"},
			{id=8058,title="Flash",body="Ka'roz charges around the raid toward random targets. All players caught in his path are afflicted by Whirling."},
			{id=8059,title="Whirling",body="Player caught in Ka'roz's path as he Flashes around spin around and suffer $143702s1 Physical damage per second. Any other players caught in the vicinity of a Whirling victim also suffer this damage."},
			{id=8060,title="Hurl Amber",body="Ka'roz will periodically jump up to one of the platforms located about the room and Hurl Amber down at his enemies. Wherever the amber lands a pool of Caustic Amber will form. Players that enter a pool of Caustic Amber will suffer $143735s1 Nature damage every second they remain in the area.\n\n$[!3,4,7,14 In non-Heroic Difficulties, Ka'roz hurls three pieces of amber.$]$[!5,6 In Heroic Difficulty Ka'roz hurls four pieces of amber and the pool of Caustic Amber persists for the duration of the encounter.$]"},
			{id=8080,title="Strong Legs",body="Players of the damage dealer role can acquire this Paragon Power. When activated the player leaps to one of the platforms Ka'roz used to Hurl Amber from. If there is an amber at the platform the player leapt to they have the opportunity to throw the amber down to create an Amber Explosion for $143967s1 Nature damage to all enemies within $143967A1 yards of the impact. If there is no amber at the platform or when the player successfully throws the amber they will jump back down automatically.\n\n$[!3,4,5,6,7,14 Hurled Amber will destroy the amber summoned by Korven to heal himself or his allies.$]"},
			{id=8011,title="Korven the Prime"},
			{id=8052,title="Encase in Amber",body="If Korven the Prime or any other active Paragon is below 50% health remaining Korven will Encase them in Amber for $142564d. If the amber is not defeated within $142564d the target will be restored to full health.\n\nThis ability cannot be used more than once every 30 seconds.\n\n$[!3,4,5,6,7,14 The explosion from the Hurl Amber ability acquired from Ka'roz after he has been defeated will destroy the amber summoned by this ability.$]\n\n$[!5,6 In Heroic Difficulties the Amber summoned by this ability is immune to all player abilities.$]"},
			{id=8053,title="Shield Bash",body="Korven the Prime slams his shield into his primary tank target, knocking them down and stunning them for $143974d. The victim is defenseless for the duration.\n\nImmediately after using Shield Bash, Korven the Prime unleashes a Vicious Assault."},
			{id=8054,title="Vicious Assault",body="Korven the Prime follows up his Shield Bash with 6 different strikes at all targets in front of him. The first strike causes the victim to suffer $143979s1 Physical damage every $143979t1 seconds. Each successive strike inflicts greater and greater Physical damage."},
			{id=8078,title="Master of Amber",body="A player of the tank role can acquire this Paragon Power. When activated the caster Encases a friendly target in Amber for $142618d. While the amber holds the target is immune to all damage."},
			{id=8012,title="Iyyokuk the Lucid"},
			{id=8055,title="Calculate",body="When Iyyokuk the Lucid enters the fight he perceives the general attributes of all players and notes the result of his calculations on each target.\n\nThese calculations are noted with a shape, a color, and a number.\n\nPossible shapes are:\n- Mantid\n- Sword\n- Staff\n- Drum\n- Bomb\n\nPossible colors are:\n- Red\n- Purple\n- Blue\n- Green\n- Yellow\n\nPossible Numbers Range from 1 to 5."},
			{id=8056,title="Diminish",body="Iyyokuk uses his command of the arcane to alter the victim's health by $143666s2% of its current value.  If the target is below 25% of their maximum health they will die instantly."},
			{id=8057,title="Insane Calculation: Fiery Edge",body="Iyyokuk peers through the veil of his previous calculations and selects an initial target, then all other targets based on the initial target's criteria to spawn lines of fire between them.  All targets and any victims caught in the lines between them suffer Fire damage every second. The damage decreases as the endpoints of the line get further away from one another.\n\n$[!3,7 In 10 Player Normal and Raid Finder Difficulties, Iyyokuk selects all targets that match one of the intial target's criteria.$]$[!14 In Flexible Raid Mode, Iyyokuk selects all targets that match either of one or two of the initial target's criteria.$]$[!4 In 25 Player Normal Difficulty, Iyyokuk selects all targets that match any of two of the initial target's three critera.$]$[!5 In 10 Player Heroic Difficulty, Iyyokuk selects all targets that match any of two of the initial target's three critera.$]$[!6 in 25 Player Heroic Difficulty, Iyyokuk selects all targets that match any of the initial target's three criteria.$]\n\n$[!5,6 In Heroic Difficulty, each target creates a line of fire between themselves and two other targets.$]"},
			{id=8079,title="Ingenious",body="Players of the healer role can acquire this Paragon Power. When activated the caster heals the initial target. The heal is then copied to other members of the raid.\n\n$[!3,4,7 In Normal and Raid Finder Difficulties the heal is copied to anyone that shares the race or class of the initial target.$]$[!5,6 In Heroic Difficulty the heal is copied to all other raid members who share the class of the initial target.$]"},
			{id=8009,title="Xaril the Poisoned Mind"},
			{id=8034,title="Toxic Injection",body="When Xaril joins the encounter, he randomly injects all players with one of three different toxins: red, blue, or yellow."},
			{id=8470,title="Caustic Blood",body="Successful melee strikes from Xaril inject a caustic poison into the victim. The injection inflicts $142315s1 Nature damage per application to the target every second for $142315d. If the injection is allowed to stack to 10, a Bloody Explosion occurs.\n\nCaustic Blood will fail to hit tanks who are using their Active Mitigation abilities."},
			{id=8471,title="Bloody Explosion",body="Allowing Caustic Blood to apply 10 times results in a Bloody Explosion, inflicting $142317s1 Fire Damage to the entire raid."},
			{id=8035,title="Tenderizing Strikes",body="Xaril's dagger strikes tenderize the flesh of his victim. Any attacks received from Kil'ruk the Wind-Reaver will inflict $142929s2% more damage for each application of Tenderizing Strikes."},
			{id=8036,title="Choose Catalyst",body="Xaril the Poisoned Mind selects a catalyst at random and strikes all members of the raid with a toxin that matches the color of the catalyst. This catalyst causes all targets' toxins to react according to the type of toxin."},
			{id=8037,title="Catalytic Reaction: Red",body="When this toxin reacts to a red catalyst it explodes for $142736s1 Fire damage to all players within $142736A1 yards.",difficultyIDs={14,15,17}},
			{id=8038,title="Catalytic Reaction: Blue",body="When this toxin reacts to a blue catalyst it explodes for $142735s1 Frost damage divided among all players within $142735A1 yards.\n\n$[!3,5 In 10 Player Difficulty, the maximum number of targets that can split the damage is limited to 2.$]$[!4,6 In 25 Player Difficulty the maximum number of targets that can split the damage is limited to 3.$]",difficultyIDs={14,15,17}},
			{id=8039,title="Catalytic Reaction: Yellow",body="When this toxin reacts to a yellow catalyst it creates a cloud of Noxious Vapors for $142737d. Player caught in the cloud suffer $142797s1 Nature damage per second.",difficultyIDs={14,15,17}},
			{id=8040,title="Catalytic Reaction: Orange",body="When either a yellow toxin or a red toxin reacts to this catalyst, a ring of Fire explodes outward. Players do not see or need to react to the ring that forms at their own feet; but must avoid those rings that are created by their allies.",difficultyIDs={16}},
			{id=8041,title="Catalytic Reaction: Purple",body="When either a blue toxin or red toxin reacts to this catalyst the victim will be forced to run forward, leaving a trail of Canned Heat in their wake for $143575d. Players stepping into the area suffer $143576s1 Fire damage every second they remain in the area.",difficultyIDs={16}},
			{id=8042,title="Catalytic Reaction: Green",body="When either a blue or yellow toxin reacts to this catalyst a small cloud of Eerie Fog will form and wander about randomly. Players who enter the area suffer $142945s1 Nature damage per second for $142945d. \n\nEntering the area Chills victims to the Bone, increasing the damage received from the Eerie Fog by $144216s1% for $144216d.\n\nEvery time a player enters the area the fog reduces in size.  When it has been reduced in size 3 times it will dissipate.",difficultyIDs={16}},
			{id=8076,title="Vast Apothecarial Knowledge",body="Players in the healer role may acquire this Paragon Power. When Apothecary: Knowledge is activated, all healing done for the next $142598d will leave a Volatile Poultice on the target for an amount equal to the healing done. The next time the target is damaged, the Volatile Poultice releases the stored healing on the target."},
			{id=8010,title="Kaz'tik the Manipulator"},
			{id=8043,title="Hungry Kunchongs",body="These Hungry Kunchongs are summoned by Kaz'tik the Manipulator. Whenever one dies Kaz'tik will summon another to take its place.",difficultyIDs={14,15,16}},
			{id=8044,title="Devour",body="When Kaz'tik the Manipulator Mesmerizes a player, a Hungry kunchong is selected to feed on the victim. While the Kunchong Feeds the victim suffers $142649s1 Physical damage and the Kunchong gains $142645s1 Energy each second. If the Kunchong suffers 30% of its total health in damage from the time it began to Feed on the victim, the Feeding will stop and the victim will be freed of the Mesmerize."},
			{id=8045,title="Devour Whole",body="Hungry Kunchongs will instantly kill any player who gets too close. The process energizes the Hungry Kunchong to full."},
			{id=8046,title="Thick Shell",body="When not in the process of Feeding, Hungry Kunchongs are immune to all damage.\n\nThe impact of the player ability, Angel of Death, gained from Kil'ruk after he has been defeated will disable a Hungry Kunchong's Thick Shell."},
			{id=8047,title="Molt",body="A Hungry Kunchong that reaches full energy will Molt. The process transforms the Hungry Kunchong into a Mature Kunchong."},
			{id=8048,title="Mature Kunchong",body="Mature Kunchongs will ignore normal attempts to control them and attack any players nearby with their newly acquired ability: Swipe."},
			{id=8049,title="Swipe",body="The Mature Kunchong swings both of its massive pincers, inflicting $142655s1 Physical damage to all targets in front of it."},
			{id=8050,title="Mesmerize",body="Kaz'tik selects a random member of the raid and forces them to walk toward one of his Hungry Kunchongs. If the victim is allowed to reach the Kunchong they will be Devoured Whole.",difficultyIDs={14,15,16}},
			{id=8051,title="Sonic Projection",body="Kaz'tik selects a random member of the raid and fires a sonic wave in their direction. Player caught in the path of the wave suffer $143768s1 Physical damage."},
			{id=8077,title="Master of Puppets",body="Players of any role may acquire this power. When activated the player summons an Immature Kunchong to fight at their side for $146890d."},
			{id=8004,title="Kil'ruk the Wind-Reaver"},
			{id=8005,title="Exposed Veins",body="Kil'ruk the Wind-Reaver's sharp blades expose the blood vessels of his victims, making them more susceptible to the attacks of Xaril the Poisoned Mind.\n\nAll damage taken from Xaril the Poisoned Mind is increased 10% for each application of Exposed Veins."},
			{id=8006,title="Gouge",body="Kil'ruk the Wind-Reaver incapacitates his current tank target.  This attack is followed immediately by Mutilate."},
			{id=8007,title="Mutilate",body="Kil'ruk the Wind-Reaver lashes out with both of his weapons for a devastating attack."},
			{id=8008,title="Death from Above",body="Kil'ruk the Wind-Reaver leaps into the air over a random player and then crashes down. Kil'ruk inflicts Physical damage to all enemies within $142232A1 yards upon landing."},
			{id=8475,title="Reave",body="Kil'ruk leaps to a random player and begins to spin in place. All players are drawn toward Kil'ruk and suffer Physical damage for $148676d. The damage each player suffers during Reave is decreased as the player gets away from Kil'ruk.",difficultyIDs={16}},
			{id=8075,title="Reave",body="Players of the damage dealer role may acquire this power. Activating this ability causes the caster to leap forward a fixed distance and inflict Physical damage to all enemies within $142272A1 yards of the impact.\n\n$[!14,15,16 If a Hungry Kunchong with a Thick Shell is in the area of impact, the Thick Shell will be disabled.$]",difficultyIDs={16}},
		},
	},
	[856]={
		encounterID=856,
		instanceID=369,
		order=7,
		name="Kor'kron Dark Shaman",
		lore="Haromm and Kardris trained thousands of shaman to whisper reverently to the elements to requisition their aid. The army of Garrosh, however, does not ask - they take what they desire in the name of the True Horde. Dark Shamanism forces the elements into servitude, twisting them into burned-out ash, corrupted waters, and toxic air.",
		dungeonEncounterID=1606,
		uiMapID=560,
		pin={x=0.4752,y=0.6095},
		difficultyIDs={14,15,16,17,241},
		npcIDs={71466,71858,71859},
		displayIDs={49176,49177},
		loot={
			{itemID=112768,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112769,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112770,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112771,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112772,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112773,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112774,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112754,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112755,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112756,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112757,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112758,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112759,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112760,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=112761,diffs={},faction=-1},
